1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:01,380
Your project folder

2
00:00:01,380 --> 00:00:01,780
can have

3
00:00:01,780 --> 00:00:02,260
a place

4
00:00:02,260 --> 00:00:03,220
for history,

5
00:00:03,220 --> 00:00:03,860
even before

6
00:00:03,860 --> 00:00:04,420
you save

7
00:00:04,420 --> 00:00:05,620
its first version.

8
00:00:05,620 --> 00:00:06,100
That is

9
00:00:06,100 --> 00:00:07,740
what initializing a Git

10
00:00:07,780 --> 00:00:09,340
repository prepares.

11
00:00:10,233 --> 00:00:11,353
Imagine a volunteer

12
00:00:11,353 --> 00:00:12,473
club newsletter,

13
00:00:12,473 --> 00:00:13,353
a draft,

14
00:00:13,353 --> 00:00:13,993
photos,

15
00:00:13,993 --> 00:00:14,633
and notes

16
00:00:14,633 --> 00:00:15,673
in one folder.

17
00:00:15,673 --> 00:00:16,713
You can initialize

18
00:00:16,713 --> 00:00:17,913
that existing folder,

19
00:00:17,913 --> 00:00:18,393
or start

20
00:00:18,393 --> 00:00:18,633
with a

21
00:00:18,633 --> 00:00:19,313
new one.

22
00:00:20,233 --> 00:00:21,033
Git adds

23
00:00:21,033 --> 00:00:22,153
its own repository

24
00:00:22,153 --> 00:00:22,873
information,

25
00:00:22,873 --> 00:00:24,473
usually inside a hidden

26
00:00:24,473 --> 00:00:26,553
folder called .git.

27
00:00:26,553 --> 00:00:27,193
This gives

28
00:00:27,193 --> 00:00:28,233
the project local

29
00:00:28,233 --> 00:00:29,593
infrastructure for tracking

30
00:00:29,593 --> 00:00:30,713
changes and storing

31
00:00:30,713 --> 00:00:31,793
recorded history.

32
00:00:32,633 --> 00:00:34,553
But initialization does not

33
00:00:34,553 --> 00:00:35,113
create your

34
00:00:35,113 --> 00:00:36,233
first commit.

35
00:00:36,233 --> 00:00:37,753
Existing files are not

36
00:00:37,753 --> 00:00:39,753
automatically staged or committed,

37
00:00:39,753 --> 00:00:40,313
and nothing

38
00:00:40,313 --> 00:00:41,113
is uploaded

39
00:00:41,113 --> 00:00:41,513
just because

40
00:00:41,513 --> 00:00:42,393
you initialize

41
00:00:42,393 --> 00:00:42,993
the folder.

42
00:00:43,900 --> 00:00:44,220
Think of

43
00:00:44,220 --> 00:00:44,540
it as

44
00:00:44,540 --> 00:00:44,940
adding an

45
00:00:44,940 --> 00:00:46,060
empty history shelf

46
00:00:46,060 --> 00:00:47,180
beside your work.

47
00:00:47,180 --> 00:00:48,940
The repository is ready,

48
00:00:48,940 --> 00:00:49,980
the history begins

49
00:00:49,980 --> 00:00:50,300
when you

50
00:00:50,300 --> 00:00:51,420
deliberately record a

51
00:00:51,420 --> 00:00:52,020
commit.
